presentation/

# Canonical tracked documentation stays in the repo. docs/ is a source-of-truth
# project asset, not private scratch, and must NOT be added to this file
# (a prior claim that docs/ was gitignored was wrong and has been corrected:
# `git ls-files docs/` returns tracked files and `git check-ignore` matches
# none of them). presentation/ (above) is the opposite:
# gitignored working material, not a canonical tracked asset.

